asically be getting rid of the  one thing that makes it very unique and  special however a stemless design would  actually be really cool because you can  change your shirt without kind of  nicking the stem on the airpods and you  can put on a motorcycle helmet and use  them while riding your motorcycle with  transparency mode turned on you still  want to hear what's around you but that  would be kind of convenient because with  the current airpods you can't really do  that however in october of last year mac  rumors received this image from a source  named xerxes with basically no track  record but it showed a new airpods pro 2  case with basically the same design  except for a couple of changes like  adding speaker holes on the bottom to  use with find my and this new little  attachment on the side for attaching  various accessories if you want to kind  of attach your air pods to your bag or  something else and then last month mac  rumors dug in a little bit deeper and  said that the airpods pro 2 are likely  to feature exactly the same design in  terms of the actual buds themselves  contrary to the stemless rumors so why  would apple do this well first of all it  is a lot cheaper to reuse the same  earbud design as they did before because  they don't have to pay for the new  manufacturing the new tooling you just  do the same thing as you did before and  apple is going to be saving a lot of  money and it's going to help the actual  supply chain as well and this is  important for apple because right now  they're trying to increase their profit  margins as much as they can because of  all of the inflationary issues that are  going on and then on top of that if  apple is able to upgrade the internals  of the actual earbuds themselves making  the speakers better making the noise  cancellation better and maybe even  adding lossless audio which i'm gonna  talk about then they could get away with  not changing the design but upgrading  them to airpods pro 2 and people are  still going to buy them and speaking of  lossless audio minchiko came out in the  beginning of this year in january saying  that the airpods pro 2 are going to  feature lossless audio support which is  a big deal because apple has basically  upgraded their entire apple music  library to support lossless audio but  right now none of the airpods support it  not even the airpods max support  lossless audio so because apple made  such a huge effort to bring all the  songs up to par with lossless audio  support and make sense for them to find  a way to make airpods at least the new  ones support lossless audio and i  actually made a video about this six  months ago talking about how apple could  be using some new chip potentially like  the u2 chip or ultra wideband or  something else to bring lossless to the  new airpods pro 2. and just a couple of  weeks ago 52 audio came out with a  massive leak saying that the airpods pro  2 will feature an upgraded h1 ship find  my support heart rate detection  usbc  and more as you can see we have the same  design for the case and the actual air  pods themselves but we're going to be  getting all these upgrades including  sound improvements as well with the  airpods pro 2 sharing the acoustics with  the airpods 3 which do have new dynamic  speaker drivers and extra capabilities  like using them as hearing aids which 52  audio thinks they are going to have and  if you haven't heard of 52audio.com  they're actually extremely accurate in  terms of their leaks because they  actually had the airpods pro first look  leak correct and accurate from the get  go which was awesome revealing the case  and the actual  earbuds and they actually had the  airpods 3 first look leak correct as  well showing off some of the components  of the air pass 3 and they were spot on  including some features like having the  h1 ship not having anc  and some of these other things as well  but the really awesome part is that they  release some images showing off  basically the same case that we saw  before in the previously leaked images  last year with some speaker holes on the  bottom which will be used for find my  and this accessory attachment on the  side but not only that you can see right  here that this is a usb c port which i  think is awesome and i really hope it  does because i was not expecting usbc  accessories to come until after the  iphone 15 lineup next year but there is  a chance that they're going to do it  earlier with the airpods pro because  these will likely be selling for the  next couple of years so they might want  to switch to usbc first before they get  forced to switch  next year by the eu and everything else  now on top of that we also got some  recent leaks from mark german saying  that the airpods pro 2 are no longer  expected to feature built-in heart rate  or body temperature sensors which is a  little bit disappointing because a lot  of people were excited for that but  apple might hold off until they redesign  it again which might not happen for a  few years who knows at this point but  just to add to the whole usb c point  minchiko actually talked about it back  in may saying that apple is going to be  switching all of their accessories  including the airpods magic keyboard  trackpad mouse mac safe battery  everything else to usbc in the  foreseeable future which i totally agree  with and i hope it happens sooner rather  than later and then finally talking  about the release date we did get some  clues from mark german saying that they  are going to be updated this fall which  i totally agree with and i think it's  going to be coming maybe in october or  november but there is a chance they  could come alongside the new iphone 14  lineup i'm not really sure but i think  it is going to be happening sometime  this fall so  if you're interested in waiting for the  airpods pro 2 i think that's going to be  an excellent choice because if these  support lossless audio that is going to  be a huge improvement compared to the  current airpods pro that do not so even  if you can get them on sale for 200  i would honestly just wait a few more  months with the air pods or earbuds that  you have now and just spend the extra  50 bucks who knows maybe they're gonna  be even more expensive three hundred  dollars i mean that'd be crazy hopefully  250 and i think that would be a great  choice now if you disagree with me let  me know down in the comment section  below but if you enjoy the video click  the circle above to subscribe for more  videos like this one and check out one  of those two right over there thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

